 "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter (via E8951 BACnet gateway)",
 "applies_to": "Veris H8437V, H8437VB and H8437VBS power meters, read through a Veris E8951 Modbus-to-BACnet protocol converter.",
 "summary": "The Veris E8951 discovers supported Veris Modbus RTU meters and presents each one as its own BACnet device on BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP, with a fixed object profile per meter type. The H8437 profile adds neutral current, frequency, kVAh/kVARh, demand and max demand, usage-time counters and voltage/current THD to the H8436-style objects.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "50000 + Modbus address",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Objects as printed in the E8951 Appendix 1 profile table; names are the table's Data Variable column (the guide does not spell out the BACnet Object_Name).",
  "The E8951 creates one virtual BACnet device per discovered Modbus meter; default device instance = 50000 + Modbus address, default device name = meter series abbreviation + \"_\" + Modbus address.",
  "The guide says 66 data objects; the table lists 68 (57 AI, 11 AV).",
  "H8437 meters run at 9600 or 19200 baud."
 ],
